WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Um, do you think that entrepreneurs are

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.480
born or created?

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:09.120
>> I think you have to have two things. You

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.240
have to have this irrational optimism

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.200
that things are going to be easier than

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:16.600
they are, and you also have to have this

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.520
this undying like believe like security

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.880
about yourself. I know so many people

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.120
who make phenomenal money simply because

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.240
they're not insecure. That's one pattern

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.400
I see across the world is that there's

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.160
people who are not that competent, not

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.840
that good looking, not that great at

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.400
sales people, whatever it might be. You

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.640
know, they're below average in almost

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.800
every area, but they can make phenomenal

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.640
money just because they're not insecure.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.320
And I think that's one of the traits of

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.520
an entrepreneur is they're

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.080
they're ready to fail, they're ready to

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.920
get out there and mix it up, and they

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.160
have this undying confidence in

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.520
themselves.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.200
>> Mhm. Where [clears throat] do you think

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.240
that comes from in your case? Is that

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.320
something that was instilled from your

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.160
family and your background, do you

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.280
think, or is it just a personality

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.200
wiring?

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.400
>> I think the one thing that was different

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.320
about me when I grew up, and I can thank

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.320
my dad for this, is that I was I was

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:05.480
raised around a kitchen table of

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:08.600
just building each other up and and and

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:10.040
optimism. And a lot of I didn't notice

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.280
it until later, until I was in high

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.760
school, and I was like after a

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.440
basketball game, I'd see my friends

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.840
their dads would just tear them down.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.800
And I don't know if you experienced

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.880
this, they'd get them in the car and

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.560
say, "You weren't hustling after this

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.800
ball. You should have made this pass

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.400
here. You messed up over here." And it

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.840
was just constant beating them down. And

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.400
look, I had my fair share of bad

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.280
basketball games, but I got in the car

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.760
and my dad said, "You know, I'm really

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.160
proud of you. You laid it on the line.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.760
Like, that was that was a good a good

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.080
day, a good game."

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.600
And that blowed up that blowed over.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:38.440
Like, my dad around the kitchen table,

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.400
and my mom as well, just made me believe

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.760
that I could do things.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.400
That I was good enough. They built me up

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:45.760
instead of tore me down.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.320
And unfortunately, I I don't know if

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:51.160
it's the majority of parents who do the

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:51.160
opposite. What's your opinion on that?

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.600
>> Man,

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:57.040
it's a it's a huge question. I think

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.400
like most things, the answer is a

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.640
combination.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:02.120
I think people like to split things into

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.120
binaries when they're not. So, there's

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.080
that whole thing of, you know, is it

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.320
nature or nurture? And I think the

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.080
reality is most human traits and

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.800
behaviors, I I'd say all of them pretty

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:15.480
much, are some combination, right? Like

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:17.920
it's not If it were just nurture, then

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.400
siblings and people from similar

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.080
backgrounds would kind of all go on to

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:22.959
do the same things, have the same

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.560
interests, achieve the same success. And

00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:25.040
we we clearly see that's not the case,

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:25.959
you know, a family

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:28.440
>> Yeah.

00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:31.400
>> I I'm one of five children, and the

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:33.160
paths myself and my siblings have taken

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.320
are quite different in a lot of ways.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.600
You could say there's actually a lot of

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.600
parallels in terms of our values and

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.040
certain ways we look at the world and

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.680
things like that in terms of like our

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.720
core values, the same core values were

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.040
instilled in us. But we we took very

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.280
different paths, we have different

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.640
interests and different personalities.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:51.480
And then,

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:54.200
obviously, like it can't all just be

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.800
nurture because there are people who are

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.440
uh hundreds of millions of people around

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:00.480
the world, maybe billions, who are

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:03.800
raised in all sorts of awful, jacked-up,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.640
messed-up situations, which on paper

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.320
is is, you know, like on objectively,

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.160
this is a bad upbringing. They have so

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:11.200
many things working against them, and

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.560
then they go out there, and some of them

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.360
achieve massive success. Other people

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.320
end up in prison, other people go out

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.600
and do some terrible thing. And then

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:20.080
there's people who are raised extremely

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.320
well, who go out and do terrible things.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.480
So,

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.800
it's

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.440
I think it's some type of like

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:28.239
everything else, I think it's just this

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:31.200
combination, and it's quite difficult to

00:03:28.239 --> 00:03:32.680
parse out how much of it is nature and

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.920
how much of it is nurture, cuz we can't

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:36.080
really run a

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:38.117
control experiment. Not in an ethical

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:39.200
way, anyway. You you kind of have

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:41.400
>> [laughter]

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.080
>> I definitely hit the lottery. Um I I was

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:45.959
passed the genetics of my father, the

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.160
charisma, a little bit of the, you know,

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:50.120
um

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:51.320
extraverted, you know, nature. But then,

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.920
I was raised around two parents who

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.840
loved each other, man. Like my dad loved

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.280
my mom, my mom loved my dad, they

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.960
supported us. We didn't ever have to

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:01.920
worry about, you know, irrational things

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:03.400
happening and just craziness in our life

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.800
that I think causes a lot of trauma and

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.560
just sets people back in a major way.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:09.440
So, you know, that's me, man. That's

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.440
That's where I came from.

